Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790643599999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790639999999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The 2850 high was not followed by a trend bar: 1790035200000 is an inside bar and 1790121600000 closed 2684.16 below its open, leaving 1790639999999 162 points under the high.", "1787270400000 left a ~256-point upper tail (high 2771 vs close 2515.3), and the following 27 bars could not exceed 2680, showing repeated failure to hold new highs.", "The final four bars are near-doji small-range bars (2636.28-2740.42), a tight two-sided cluster at the trend extreme that fits a final-flag shape rather than trend resumption.", "Two earlier vertical spikes in this window (1787097600000, 1787270400000) were each followed by multi-week ranges, so a stall after the 2850 high is consistent with this window's prior behavior."], "evidence_for": ["Progression of higher swing highs and higher swing lows over the last 40 bars: lows 2357.18 (1788307200000), 2358.62 (1789430400000), 2436.87 (1789689600000) and 2633.31 (1790208000000).", "1789689600000-1789948800000 broke above the 27-bar range and above the prior 2771 spike high, with closes near the highs and acceptance above 2612.02.", "The last seven bars hold entirely above the 2612.02 breakout close and above the 2436.87 breakout-low; no bear bar has closed below a prior bull swing low.", "Buying continued after each consolidation: ranges following the 2293.8/2771 spike highs and after the 27-bar range were all resolved upward."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window opens at 2006.31 (1780272000000) and sells off to a 1368.42 low (1780704000000) on bars that close near their lows.", "Price then recovers into a long overlapping range around 1710-1975 (e.g. 1692.84 low at 1782000000000 to 1974.46 high at 1785110400000) that persists until 1787011200000.", "1787097600000 is a large bull trend bar (open 1916.51, high 2293.8, close 2252.16), followed by closes of 2326.32 (1787184000000) and 2515.3 with a 2771 high (1787270400000): a three-bar vertical bull spike.", "From 1787356800000 to 1789603200000 the market holds a 27-bar two-sided range between 2357.18 (1788307200000 low) and 2680 (1789084800000 high), repeatedly rejecting 2520-2557 and 2357-2400 with heavy body overlap.", "1789689600000-1789948800000 breaks above that range and above the 2771 spike high: closes 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.9, 2775.61, with the 2850 high at 1789948800000.", "The new high lacks strong follow-through: 1790035200000 is an inside bar and 1790121600000 closes 2684.16 below its open.", "The last seven bars (1790035200000-1790553600000) are overlapping, with the final four trading 2636.28-2740.42 and 1790639999999 closing 2687.88, roughly mid-range and 162 below the 2850 high."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Multi-month bull swing from the 1368.42 low to the 2850 high, with successively higher swing lows (1512.91, 1533.12, 2357.18, 2436.87, 2633.31) across the supplied window.", "end_time_ms": 1790639999999, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "1368.42", "start_time_ms": 1780704000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Three-bar vertical bull spike following a long two-sided range: open 1916.51 to close 2252.16 (1787097600000), close 2326.32 (1787184000000), then a 2771 high with a 2515.3 close and a large upper tail (1787270400000).", "end_time_ms": 1787270400000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "1905.63", "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": "2771"}, {"description": "Twenty-seven-bar two-sided range after the spike: repeated highs 2520-2557 plus the 2680 spike high at 1789084800000, and repeated lows 2357-2400 with 2357.18 at 1788307200000 and 2358.62 at 1789430400000; no sustained close beyond either edge.", "end_time_ms": 1789603200000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Four-bar bull breakout above the 27-bar range and above the 2771 spike high, closing near highs at 2612.02, 2632.98, 2642.9 and 2775.61, with the 2850 high printed at 1789948800000.", "end_time_ms": 1789948800000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2436.87", "start_time_ms": 1789689600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Tight seven-bar consolidation just under the 2850 high; the last four bars are small overlapping dojis traded between 2636.28 and 2740.42, with no close beyond the 2612.02 breakout close and final close 2687.88.", "end_time_ms": 1790639999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790035200000, "upper_boundary": "2786.81"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Bull continuation: a close above 2786.81 and then 2850 on a trend bar with follow-through, and a higher low above 2633.31, would confirm resumption of the bull channel.", "A bear body closing below 2633.31 and then below the 2612.02 breakout close would suggest the breakout has failed and shift the read toward a trading range or transition-unclear.", "A close below 2436.87 would break the most recent bull swing low and question the always-in-long classification.", "Continued overlapping bars contained between 2633.31 and 2786.81 with no boundary close would keep the current read of a bull trend in a breakout-mode tight range."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790639999999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["The window's dominant move is the 21% bull leg (2358.62 to 2850) and the window closes +8.0%, so the sideways stretch can be read as a bull flag or a pause in a bull channel rather than a completed range.", "Rising swing lows (2358.62 at 1789488000000, 2633.31 at 1790236800000, 2636.28 at 1790582400000) are consistent with support rising inside an ongoing bull channel.", "Four of the last five bars closed up (2667.86, 2677.55, 2672.79, 2687.88) after a bull reversal bar at 1790582400000 that closed at its high, so the immediate leg has bullish direction even while the band holds.", "The lower-high sequence is only three to four highs deep and price never broke below 2633.31, so an 'mtr-like' topping read is unconfirmed rather than established."], "evidence_for": ["The ~45 bars since 1789992000000 stay inside 2633.31-2804.59 with overlapping bodies and repeated reversal bars (1790164800000 open 2726.71/close 2659.00, 1790323200000 close 2715.90, 1790568000000 close 2645.21) - range behavior rather than trend behavior.", "Post-spike highs decline (2804.59, 2786.81, 2740.42, 2718.83) and the 2850 spike high is still untested, so there is no bull follow-through after the spike.", "Net change over the post-spike stretch is negative (close 2754.31 at 1789992000000 vs 2687.88 at decision time), even though the full 120-bar window is up.", "The last 20 bars cover only 2636.28-2718.83 (~3%) with small overlapping bars, which is consistent with a tight range in breakout mode."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed H4 bars from 1788912000000 to 1790639999999; first close 2487.82, final close 2687.88 (+8.0% across the window).", "Window's dominant leg is bullish: from the low 2358.62 at bar 1789488000000 to the high 2850 at bar 1789977600000 (~21% over 35 bars), built from overlapping bull bars with shallow pullbacks (e.g., closes 2578.60 at 1789732800000, 2636.28 at 1789747200000, 2723.15 at 1789977600000).", "Earlier context: bar 1789128000000 spiked to 2680 but closed 2555.52, price gave it back and a bear leg ran to 2358.62 (bar 1789488000000) before the bull leg began.", "Bar 1789977600000 is the widest bar of the window (open 2658.81, high 2850, low 2658.06, close 2723.15; range 191.94) and closes 126.85 below its high - a spike/climax-type bar at the end of the bull leg.", "No high after that bar exceeds 2804.59 (bar 1790020800000); successive swing highs step down: 2804.59 (1790020800000), 2786.81 (1790136000000), 2740.42 (1790323200000), 2718.83 (1790496000000).", "From bar 1789992000000 to the decision time, no bar closes above 2775.61 or below 2645.21; price stays inside 2633.31 (bar 1790236800000 low) - 2804.59 (bar 1790020800000 high).", "Lower supports retested and held: lows 2648.49 (bar 1790164800000), 2633.31 (1790236800000), 2637 (1790568000000), 2636.28 (1790582400000).", "Last 20 bars (1790352000000-1790639999999) hold inside 2636.28 (bar 1790582400000 low) - 2718.83 (bar 1790496000000 high), an ~82.5 point (~3%) band with small, heavily overlapping bodies and closes near mid-range.", "Most recent sequence: bull reversal bar 1790582400000 (open 2645.21, low 2636.28, close 2667.86 = high) followed by closes 2677.55, 2672.79, 2687.88; the final high 2691.43 remains below the 2718.83 swing high."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "trading-range", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Bull leg / stair-step channel from the 2358.62 low at bar 1789488000000 to the 2850 high at bar 1789977600000 (~21% over 35 bars); shallow pullbacks and persistent higher swing lows until the final spike bar. This is the window's dominant directional leg.", "end_time_ms": 1789991999999, "kind": "channel", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Wide spike bar at 1789977600000 (open 2658.81, high 2850, low 2658.06, close 2723.15, range 191.94) closing 126.85 below its high. Marks a spike/climax that ends the bull leg; it does not by itself reverse the trend.", "end_time_ms": 1789991999999, "kind": "climax", "lower_boundary": "2658.06", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Post-spike trading range from bar 1789992000000 to the decision time, bounded by 2633.31 and 2804.59: heavy bar overlap, repeated reversals and no follow-through beyond the band. The 2850 spike high has not been retested in ~45 bars.", "end_time_ms": 1790639999999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1789992000000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}, {"description": "Tight balance of the last 20 bars (1790352000000-1790639999999) inside 2636.28-2718.83 (~82.5 points, ~3% wide) with small overlapping bodies and closes near mid-range; both edges have been touched, so the breakout direction is unresolved.", "end_time_ms": 1790639999999, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2636.28", "start_time_ms": 1790352000000, "upper_boundary": "2718.83"}, {"description": "Possible lower-high sequence after the 2850 spike high (2804.59 -> 2786.81 -> 2740.42 -> 2718.83) plus a strong bear bar at 1790164800000 (open 2726.71, close 2659.00). Unconfirmed: lows keep holding above 2633.31 and no lower low below the band has printed.", "end_time_ms": 1790639999999, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Acceptance above 2718.83 (a close above it followed by a second close above 2740.42) would shift the read toward bull-trend / breakout with follow-through.", "A close below 2633.31 that holds under 2636.28 and 2622.67 would signal downward resolution of the range and activate the mtr-like lower-high sequence.", "Continued small overlapping bars between 2636.28 and 2718.83 keep the tight-range / breakout-mode classification unchanged.", "A strong bull close back above 2804.59, especially a retest of 2850, would revive the bull-trend read and make the post-spike range look like a bull flag."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2673.99", "close_time_ms": 1